WEBVTT

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.320
“There are no bad customers.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.080
Only bad stores.”

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.270
— Martin B. Stone

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.340
Welcome back, Master.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:14.940
Fortune Café.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:20.420
Though its facilities may be minimal, it's a place where the customer's every wish is granted.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:26.840
Even the most grand and luxurious cafés are nothing but
empty shacks if they don't provide what the customer seeks.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:36.370
What'cha doin' over here mister?

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:37.760
Homework.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.540
Really?!

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.420
Do you mind if I copy just the math assignment?!

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:43.370
The whole thing's math, though.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:44.360
Details...

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.840
Scoot over.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.740
Just sit across from me.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:53.270
Aww, but then I'd be looking at it upside down, and I might mess up.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.370
It would have been fine.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.870
It would so have not!

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.000
What if I mistake a 9 for a 6,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.540
or the “yo” in katakana for the letter “E”?!

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:07.770
Wait, what if the European writing system came
about because someone wrote the letters wrong?

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:11.390
If that's true, then it'd be the discovery of the century!

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.130
Katakana doesn't exist outside of Japan.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.760
Whatever. Just hurry up and copy it.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.810
Thanks a bunch!

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.910
A café where I can be alone with Arashiyama!

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:33.130
I must be in heaven!

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:33.570
Hmm?

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.370
Uh, n-nothing...

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:42.730
Men desperately seek happiness, but
happiness does not come looking for them.

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:47.050
For seldom does happiness visit men of its own volition.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:51.050
Pull the head twice, and it slides up.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.060
Arashiyama.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.530
You copied someone's homework, didn't you?

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.590
What?!

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.230
Most of your answers are correct.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.960
That's a baseless accusation!

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.140
I can do my homework when I have to.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:13.070
But you wrote the letter “I” instead of “1”.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:20.900
That aside, did you not find it odd when you wrote I=0 or 1=0?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.960
Umm, well...

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:23.790
So what?

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.410
I'll see you in the teacher's lounge after school!

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:36.430
Man! The one time I decide to do my homework and this happens.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.640
You got what you deserved.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:42.280
If I have to sit through another one of his lectures, I'll be late for work.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.400
Oh, you have a job?

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.510
Yeah. I work at a nearby café as a maid.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.050
You mean a maid café?!

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.360
Yup, exactly!

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:53.480
I just started recently, though.

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.480
Wow, that's pretty cool.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.120
They finally opened up a café near here, huh?

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:02.270
Gosh, I've always loved maid cafés.

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.830
Sipping tea and chatting with cute little maids.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:09.000
Hey Arashiyama-san, would you mind if I came by?

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.800
Sure, sure! We get so few customers, you'll practically have the place to yourselves!

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.050
Yay!

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:20.810
Although, it's run by a grannie from the neighborhood, so it might not be what you'd normally expect.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.440
One's expectations always lead to one of two harsh realities.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.440
Expectations born from anxiety often result in fearfulness,

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:32.450
while high expectations often result in betrayal.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.990
Maid Café “Seaside”.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.580
I'm sure this is the right place, though.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.580
This isn't what I expected...

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.710
Normally, no one would expect <i>this</i>.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.970
Heya!

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:51.050
Come on in!

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.490
You girls friends of Hotori's?

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.660
Yup. Come on guys, have a seat!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:02.180
There's nobody else here, so sit wherever you want.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:03.910
Let's see what's on the menu today...

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.960
Oh, I know! We got some mincemeat cutlets from Mr. Murakami.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:07.650
How's that sound?

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.690
T-Tatsuno-san?

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:13.610
You...

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:14.280
Hmm?

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.700
You call this...

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.200
a maid café?!

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.950
What the hell is “heya”? Are you a sushi joint or something?

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.090
D-did I say that?

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:32.670
You did!

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:36.430
Maid cafés have certain ways to greet their customers, you know!

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:40.070
Hmm. Howdy! Welcome to our maid café!

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:42.220
No! No! NO!

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:43.930
Listen, here's how it's supposed to go.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:48.810
Not from the throat or the belly, but from the chest, like so:

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.190
Welcome home, Master!

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:59.240
The maids I've seen on TV act just like that!

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.490
That's just the basics. Now you try.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.120
Aww, do I have to?

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.960
Don't “aww” me!

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.560
Men will come in droves if you do it right.

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:11.680
You can't just dress up and call yourself a maid!

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.300
I'm cool with just the uniform.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.140
Hey, you're pretty good!

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.810
How about you work here instead of Hotori?

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:26.390
I'd love to, but I won't have time since I've decided to join a club.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.480
We're gonna join the table tennis club.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:33.610
But in exchange, the least I could do is train Arashiyama-san for you.

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:36.400
But I don't wanna do training!

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:39.670
I can't possibly allow this crude little shop to call itself a maid café!

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:43.330
Hotori, just think of it as on the job training, okay?

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:47.160
But I really don't care for the basics.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:49.830
Mind telling me why you're working as a maid then?

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.590
Oh, good timing. Here comes the first catch of the day.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.050
The guy from the cleaners, huh?

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.880
This will be your training.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:00.590
Instant maid course, lesson one.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:01.550
The maid's greeting!

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.470
Go on, just like I showed you.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:06.850
Ehh, seriously?

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:10.020
There's no better practice than the real thing! Go get 'em!

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:14.830
Now!

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:16.570
You can do it, Arashiyama-san!

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:21.040
Wel-

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.160
Wel?

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.410
W-wel-

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:29.710
W-Welcome home, Mathter!

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.170
Tatsuno-san, she fudged it!

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:35.210
She's still okay!

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:38.040
In fact, her clumsiness made it that more effective!

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.050
Strike!

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:44.680
I'M HOME, DAISY!!!

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:47.230
Who the heck are you calling Daisy?!

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.190
See? Knocked him outta the park!

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.690
Old guys around here are defenseless against that kind of charm, huh?

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:01.700
Granny's special trick is more like shooting the moon.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.030
Instant maid course, lesson two.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:05.030
The clumsy maid!

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:08.030
Arashiyama-san doesn't really need help being clumsy, though.

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.540
You can say that again...

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.740
Aren't you guys being just a bit rude now?

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.370
It's precise control of one's clumsiness that makes a proper maid.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.240
Master it with both body and mind!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.270
Can I order now, please?

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:23.570
Guatemalan blend, piping hot please.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.680
This is it, Arashiyama-san!

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:28.240
But how am I supposed to be clumsy?

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.670
Don't worry. Leave it to me.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:32.400
Order up.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:37.270
Now, Harihara-san!

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:37.980
Gotcha!

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:48.600
IT BUUUURNS!!!

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.080
Hey, isn't that a little harsh?

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.050
She even pulled off a clumsy combo!

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.420
She's a prodigy!

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.370
What the heck are you doing, huh?!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:58.510
That was beautiful, Arashiyama-san!

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:00.920
Now take this bucket and run as fast as you can!

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.560
I'm so sorry! I'll clean it up right away!

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:04.930
Perfect, right there.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.340
Trip!

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:18.700
She nailed a 3-hit combo this time!

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:21.020
We must have been graced by the gods!

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:23.820
The god of comedy rather than maids, that is.

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:26.670
Or maybe the god of rage!

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:29.680
Do you have a grudge or something?!

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:32.790
It's your fault for compounding your clumsiness!

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.040
Is the Guatemalan ready yet?

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.210
What's going on? It's pretty busy for a change.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:42.400
Hey, we've got another bite! Greet the boy properly now!

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.710
Sanada...-kun?

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.630
How come you're all wet?

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:52.220
I'm dripping wet 'cause I'm a good girl.

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:54.430
Did Mr. Moriaki chew you out already?

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.020
Oops, I forgot.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:59.360
Don't tell him you copied me, or else I'll get yelled at too!

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:02.360
A moment, Arashiyama-san.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:05.030
W-what's up?

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:10.390
If I'm not mistaken, that was attendance number 9, Sanada-kun, right?

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:13.910
Yeah, that's him. I don't know his number though.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:16.560
How does he know about this place?

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:17.750
Why is he here?

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:18.900
Does he come often?

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:24.880
Sanada's the son of the fishmonger in this
neighborhood, so he comes by pretty often.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:25.720
Why?

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:30.690
Now that I think about it, this maid café's actually quite wonderful!

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.550
Head Maid!

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.920
I'm the owner to you.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.440
My name is Tatsuno Toshiko.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.240
Please hire me as a maid!

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:41.860
What?!

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.040
Tatsuno-san, what about our club?

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.360
We're in the table tennis club, remember?

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:51.780
I found my divine calling!

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:54.970
This will make us a full-fledged maid café.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.750
But we'll have more employees than customers.

00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:02.170
Fortune Café.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:07.380
Though its facilities may be minimal, it's a place where the customer's every wish is granted.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.970
Where is Arashiyama?

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:22.480
The words “after school” carry with them both a feeling of excitement, and a tiny bit of loneliness.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:26.110
For it is a sign that the day is nearing its end.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:30.170
All righty, let's get ready for another big day!

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:32.870
This is when your day begins?

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:37.370
Hey, Sanada. Tatsuno-san will be part-timing with me starting today!

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:39.750
Huh? You guys were serious about that?

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:43.140
Not quite, I'm still waiting for my clothes to be finished.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.530
Granny Uki said she's been sewing all day.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.610
Wow, those are hand made?

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.430
See ya later!

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.750
Feel free to come by if you want!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:54.640
Y-yeah, sure.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.560
Hey, you two.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.900
You wouldn't happen to be violating school regulations by working, would you?

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:09.220
How did our teacher find out?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.830
No idea.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:12.070
All we can do now...

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:13.280
...is run for it!

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:17.030
Hey! Stay put!

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:23.490
Shoot, I've lost them.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.540
I could have sworn they came this way.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.930
Is this really supposed to fool him?

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:31.510
Stay cool! It's perfectly normal for statues to be at a temple.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:34.410
It's a mind trick. Nobody will notice.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.180
Where on Earth did they go?!

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:41.180
I better pick up some toilet paper soon.

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:44.270
Man, thanks to him, we're late!

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.060
I hope I didn't keep Sanada-kun waiting!

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.610
Sorry we're late, Head Maid!

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:50.940
Welcome!

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:53.430
Oh Granny, you don't need to say that to us!

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.390
Are you going senile already?

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:56.920
Like hell I am.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.600
I'm talking to the customer right behind you!

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:02.260
Customer? There's no cust-

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:03.580
Oh crap!

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:07.060
Honestly, did you think you could
lose me that easily? How ridiculous.

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:08.140
Teacher...

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:10.840
As stated in clause 8 of the student handbook:

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.710
Unauthorized part-time jobs are against school regulations.

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:17.280
Item #21: If a student wishes to work,

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:20.950
they must have their guardian's approval
and submit it to their homeroom teacher.

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:22.610
My head hurts...

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:24.230
Help me, brother!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.800
Teacher, please stop!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.600
Arashiyama-san's brain is reaching critical mass!

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.820
Spare me, Mr. Mikuriya!

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:34.000
Who the hell is Mikuriya?! My name is Moriaki!

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.000
Anyway, I will not allow any work unapproved by the school!

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:40.370
Nobody follows the rules anyway!

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.270
Man, he's hard-headed! Definitely a math teacher!

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:47.390
This has been bugging me for a while,

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:50.920
but how did Mr. Moriaki learn about our job?

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:54.410
Come to think of it, just how did that leak anyway?

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.300
Could there be a spy?

00:14:56.300 --> 00:15:00.930
Hey, Sanada. Tatsuno-san will be part-timing with me starting today!

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:02.970
That was it!

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:05.110
Nobody “leaked” it, he heard you say it!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:06.600
So then, this is my fault?

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:09.570
You're as dumb as they come.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:13.310
At this point, all we can do is obtain permission!

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:16.580
That's right. I didn't come here to make you quit.

00:15:16.580 --> 00:15:20.140
But do you think we can get
permission for working at a maid café?

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:22.200
We don't have a choice.

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:23.450
We'll use maid-jutsu.

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:24.450
Maid-jutsu?

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:28.190
Serving guests in an elegant, yet illusive manner, guarantees profits.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.590
Such is the way of maid-jutsu.

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:31.320
This is the idea behind maid cafés!

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.000
And that doesn't bother your conscience?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:34.840
Quiet!

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.880
It's a showdown between the maid's
charm and the teacher's stubbornness.

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:39.090
Yin and Yang!

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:40.300
Good and evil!

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:41.750
White and black!

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.220
Dog and monkey!

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.340
There's no way I'll submit to you!

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.460
This kind of work may seem like a silly diversion to him,

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:52.150
but for me, this is the café that Sanada frequents!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.240
I've finally found my Fortune Café!

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.720
Head Maid! Is my outfit ready?

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.240
Yeah, it's on a hanger in the back.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:07.920
Arashiyama, let's suit up for war!

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.120
Fine...

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:13.130
Salmon is actually a white-flesh fish.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:16.060
It's been 22 minutes since she said that.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:19.160
It takes time for a lady to prepare.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.760
Thanks for waiting!

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:27.570
Maid #2. I'll be in your care starting today, Master!

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.980
I guess that makes me Maid #1.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:33.730
Please ask of us whatever you wish, Master.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:36.050
I lost!

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:37.070
Arashiyama-san?!

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:40.400
I've lost in academics, beauty, and style!

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:43.200
And now a crushing defeat in maid appearance!

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.640
Get a grip, Arashiyama-san!

00:16:44.640 --> 00:16:47.170
You're forgetting the real enemy!

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.950
What good am I?

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.790
Well, you do excel in one area that Tatsuno does not.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:54.590
Huh?

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:58.920
The one thing that you excel in is...

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:03.440
Am I reading into this too much,

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.390
or does he actually love me?

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:09.640
Arashiyama, you will forever win over Tatsuno with...

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:12.870
...your eyesight.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:13.770
Oh...

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:16.260
How cruel...

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:17.240
A teacher, out of all people,

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:21.170
tells me that I fail in every area compared to her, except for eyesight!

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:23.690
Arashiyama-san! Arashiyama-san!!!

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:29.160
Before we even had a chance to strike, he's crushed her confidence, the cornerstone of maid-jutsu!

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:30.620
He's a maid-killer!

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:35.040
This man is a formidable opponent!

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.350
Tatsuno-san.

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:37.840
Y-yes sir!

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:39.990
I'd like a cup of black tea.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.330
Right away.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.550
I win!

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:45.760
He's trying to test me, but it'll backfire!

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.570
Black tea is my number one specialty!

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:50.850
I'll pour him the perfect tea worthy of a maid!

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:54.300
Head Maid, what kinds of black tea do we have?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.150
Nada.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:56.990
“Nada” kind?

00:17:56.990 --> 00:17:59.040
I don't think I've heard of that kind before...

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:01.610
No, she means we don't serve tea here.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.860
W-what?! You don't serve tea?!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:08.110
Cake and tea are the staples of a maid café!

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:10.340
When you think maids, you think England!

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:11.560
When you think England, you think gentlemen!

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:13.250
When you think gentlemen, you think tea!

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:17.260
I don't like tea. Besides, it's a hassle to make anyway.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:20.000
Do you have any idea what the third kanji in “café” means?!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.840
It's “tea”, as in “black tea”!

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:24.380
But the “café” in “maid café” means coffee, doesn't it?

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:26.720
Ohhh! That's not what it means!

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:29.500
I don't really “get” tea anyways.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.450
Like Little Gray, and stuff...

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:32.930
You're thinking of aliens!

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.730
Are you referring to Earl Grey?

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:37.180
Yeah. I've also heard of Tard-jeeling.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.840
You're the retard here!

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.940
Were you trying to say Darjeeling?

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:43.490
His defense is flawless!

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:46.180
While ours is full of holes.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.400
We're in bad shape!

00:18:47.840 --> 00:18:50.580
I know! In that case, I'll turn the tables on him!

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:55.630
Arashiyama-san, I don't care what it is,
but go do one of your klutzy moves!

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:57.130
Ehhh?

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:58.630
Just apply what you've learned.

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:00.590
You can do it!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.260
If Arashiyama-san's clumsiness works...

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:07.430
We don't serve tea, so you'll have to settle for coffee, okay?

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:11.510
If it works, we can capitalize on that chance!

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:12.510
Enjoy.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:19.440
If it works, you'll have mastered maid-jutsu!

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:24.510
Ah! The coffee's fizzing over!

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:28.660
Oh, silly me! I brought you soda instead of coffee!

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:30.460
Nice, Arashiyama-san!

00:19:30.460 --> 00:19:34.080
If nothing else, your clumsiness made my heart skip a beat!

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:36.120
I'll fix that right away! Tee hee!

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:37.920
Hold on, Arashiyama.

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:43.200
Coffee is made in a siphon or a coffee machine.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:47.650
I'd like you to tell me how you managed to
mistake a coffee maker for a soda dispenser.

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:50.390
Huh? Um, well...

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:51.010
Well?

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:54.550
Well, they kind of look the same...

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:55.800
Did you do it on purpose?

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.570
N-no... I-

00:19:57.570 --> 00:19:59.190
Did you do it on purpose?

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.270
I did it on purpose. I'm sorry!

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.580
He's lecturing her over that?

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.610
Mr. Moriaki's immune to clumsiness too?

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:10.810
Have a seat right over there, Arashiyama.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:11.980
Y-yes sir...

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:16.600
Why would you do something so
senseless? I don't understand it at all.

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.810
Your behavior is simply irrational.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:19.510
Yes sir...

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:23.520
And besides, do you realize what a maid's job really is?

00:20:23.520 --> 00:20:26.510
In what universe does a maid take
pleasure in pulling pranks on her customers?

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:27.420
Yes...

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:29.570
None sir...

00:20:29.570 --> 00:20:33.150
He's completely forgotten about
not getting permission, hasn't he?

00:20:33.150 --> 00:20:37.010
The moment he began lecturing her was when Arashiyama-san became victorious!

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:40.270
That reminds me, Sanada-kun's awful late today...

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.690
Why is my homeroom teacher here?

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.320
This isn't funny.

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:47.440
Our café for two,

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:51.690
my Fortune Café... has changed.

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:53.650
You're always like this!

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:57.860
Do you not realize that stuff like 1=0 makes absolutely no sense?!

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.960
Absurd! You're completely nonsensical!

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:04.550
Men desperately seek happiness, but
happiness does not come looking for them.

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:07.960
For seldom does happiness visit men of its own volition.

00:22:36.170 --> 00:22:38.520
Thank you very maid for coming!

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:44.350
Peter Piper picked a peck of pickled peppers.

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:47.020
Fortune Café.

00:22:47.020 --> 00:22:52.020
Though its facilities may be minimal, it's a place where the customer's every wish is granted.

00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:58.570
Even the most grand and luxurious of cafés are nothing but empty shacks if they do not provide what the customer seeks.

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:04.120
Black tea, please.

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:07.960
Sorry for the wait.

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:10.790
What in the world is going on?

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:23.970
Welcome home, Master.

00:23:23.970 --> 00:23:27.590
Isn't it awful, Master? That we could be your maids...

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:31.020
Once you open that door, you can never escape...

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:32.600
What the?!

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:36.040
Please, come in. All the way in...

00:23:36.610 --> 00:23:41.000
Welcome... to your Fortune Café.

00:23:42.180 --> 00:23:44.500
My boss is such a dirtbag.

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:48.510
I thought I would ruin him by getting
him charged with sexual harassment.

00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:50.590
Isn't that a bit overkill?

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:54.660
But the jerk never takes the bait I lay for him!

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:57.950
Finally, I just flipped up my skirt I was wearing right in his face, and showed him my lingerie!

00:23:57.950 --> 00:23:59.810
You're pretty outrageous.

00:23:59.810 --> 00:24:02.040
But he got me charged for sexually harassing him instead.

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:03.630
You screwed yourself over?!

00:24:03.950 --> 00:24:07.460
Next time: Sexual Harassment Court is Super Cool!

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:10.470
Today's not over yet.
